   _Assembly.Molecular_mass                    17139.69
   _Assembly.Enzyme_commission_number          .
   _Assembly.Details
;
K63-linked diubiquitin, in which two ubiquitin molecules are linked 
via an isopeptide bond between the carboxyl group of Gly76 of the 
distal ubiquitin and the epsilon-amine of Lys63 of the proximal ubiquitin. 
The diubiquitin was made from recombinant ubiquitin monomers containing 
chain terminating mutations, K63R in the distal ubiquitin and Asp77 as 
the C-terminal extension of the proximal ubiquitin, using controlled 
enzymatic assembly of polyubiquitin chains. 
The chain terminating Asp77 on the proximal ubiquitin was then cleaved 
off by the deubiquitinase Yuh1.
;
   _Assembly.DB_query_date                     .
   _Assembly.DB_query_revised_last_date        .

